 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532952,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the lengths of the unknown sides of the <span data-math=\"{30^ \\circ } {\\text{-}} {60^ \\circ } {\\text{-}} {90^ \\circ }\">{30^ \\circ } {\\text{-}} {60^ \\circ } {\\text{-}} {90^ \\circ }</span> triangle shown..<br>\n\n<img src=\"exercises/media/2e75511b7a42da46.png\" alt=\"A right triangle. The legs are labeled a and b. The hypotenuse is labeled 5. The angles at the bottom-left and bottom-right are labeled 30 degrees and 90 degrees.\">\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The set of ratios in a 30°-60°-90° triangle are <span data-math=\"1:\\sqrt 3 :2\"></span>, or <span data-math=\"x:x\\sqrt 3 :2x\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Since you are shown the right angle and the 30° angle, you know the unmarked angle is a 60° angle.</p>\n<p>The longest side is 5, so <span data-math=\"2x = {\\text{ }}5\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"x = {\\text{ }}2.5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"x\\sqrt 3 = 2.5\\sqrt 3 \"></span></p>\n<p>The missing side lengths are <span data-math=\"a = {\\text{ }}2.5\"></span> and  <span data-math=\"b = 2.5\\sqrt 3 \"></span>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "\n<span data-math=\"\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {a = 2.5} \\\\ \n  {b = 2.5\\sqrt 3 } \n\\end{array}\">\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {a = 2.5} \\\\ \n  {b = 2.5\\sqrt 3 } \n\\end{array}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
